                <pb facs="0300" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1154/272.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Reid to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-12-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 31, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1126.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the department’s cable,
                    November 6, and subsequent correspondence in regard to the settlement of the
                    Alsop claim, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of a note from the
                    foreign office, dated the 30th instant, stating that His Majesty the King will
                    have much pleasure in acting as mediator for the adjustment of this dispute.
                    This decision has also been communicated to the Chilean minister in London by
                    Sir Edward Grey.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitelaw Reid.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d145-a1.xml" xpointer="d145-a1"/>
